comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-15T18:53:26.967Z",codex-agent,Implementation and real-repository regression evidence linked. Review remains with the orchestrator; this item stays in progress.
  "2026-10-15T18:54:04.606Z",codex-agent,Git merge-tree executes configured pm item and history drivers. Two independently added SDK comments both survive in the merged item and history tree. Replacing the item driver with a failing command yields a tracker-path conflict. Driver receipts precede Git output; the predictor parses the NUL-delimited tree record and retains every unresolved tracker path. No source history is repaired or rewritten by simulation.
  "2026-10-15T19:02:32.565Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: replaced only predict with the pre-feature no-conflict behavior. The real three-lane same-line conflict regression failed with ERR_ASSERTION, exit 1. Restored exact function bytes. Disjoint-file and tracker-driver predictions pass in the complete suite."
  "2026-10-15T19:11:53.235Z",codex-agent,"Base-update regression passes 1/1 on real Git: after a lane fast-forwards newer base commits then edits its own file, status lists only the lane file and no inherited-base drift. Reverting only status to the recorded starting base makes this test fail with ERR_ASSERTION, exit 1. Exact source bytes restored."
  "2026-10-15T19:35:54.457Z",codex-agent,"Round 1: add lane identities to predictions and compact conflict-only status with clean pair counts; full output retains commit and tree evidence."
  "2026-10-15T19:44:00.310Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: restoring only the previous status function makes the named-conflict regression fail, exit 1: three predictions instead of one compact conflict. Fixed function restored exactly. Regression also checks lane IDs/branches, base identity, conflicting files, clean pair count, and full SHA/tree fields."
  "2026-10-15T19:51:36.057Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 PM-linked acceptance: pm test pm-swarm-4343 --run --progress passed 2 linked command(s), 11 tests, zero failures. Full post-run snapshots unchanged: two registered worktrees, zero parallel branches, zero swarm Git configuration keys. Source, tracker and settings mutations remained inside scratch repositories."
  "2026-10-15T21:07:01.172Z",codex-agent,"Round 3: verified conflict status is inferred solely from path count. Reproduce a real Git conflict with no unmerged paths, preserve exit status and messages, and exercise status, ordering and landing refusal with behavioural revert proof."
  "2026-10-15T21:15:06.106Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 behavioural revert proofs on real Git 2.53.0: an even directory split plus a new file in the old directory yields merge-tree exit 1 with an empty --name-only conflict list. Fixed status retains clean=false and the directory-rename-split message; ordering returns no clean order and execute leaves the base and merge state unchanged. Individually restoring only predict, status, or cleanOrder from c086605 fails node --test --test-name-pattern=\"directory split conflict without paths\" test/review-r3.test.ts (each exit 1). Restoring only landLanes fails both node --test --test-name-pattern=\"landing rechecks\" test/review-r3.test.ts scenarios (exit 1): old code attempts an actual conflicted merge after a real linked test changes merge configuration; fixed code refuses during preflight or execution recheck. Exact function bytes restored after each control. No SDK or Git mocks."
  "2026-10-15T21:32:46.737Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 final acceptance: pm test pm-swarm-4343 --run --progress passed 4/4 linked commands and 15/15 reported tests (10 + 1 + 2 + 2), with zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo. npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed in ordinary and CI-like environments: every run passed 81/81 suite tests plus 1/1 packed npm/npx and native Bun/bunx acceptance. CI-like runs used a fresh HOME, CI=true, GITHUB_ACTIONS=true, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1. All 20 configured source files measured 100% statements, branches, functions and lines at unchanged thresholds. Identity, types, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), package contents, generated changelog and publish attestation passed. Revert evidence is recorded above; exact source restored before the matrix. Existing development-toolchain advisory remains tracked separately. No new pm CLI or SDK defect observed. Item stays in progress for orchestrator review; claim released at handoff."
